Integration

Purpose

The technology systems of the pack must function as one interconnected progression.

Each major mod has a defined role, but progression should frequently require materials, machines, processing systems, power infrastructure, logistics, and automation from multiple mods.

The purpose of integration is to prevent isolated mod progression and create meaningful cross-mod dependencies.

Cross-Mod Dependencies

Major progression stages should require multiple technological systems.

GregTech remains the primary progression backbone, while other mods provide specialized systems that become increasingly important as progression advances.

Progression should not require the player to use every mod at every stage.

Instead, each mod should become relevant when its systems solve problems created by increasing industrial complexity.

Material Progression

Materials should be shared between technological systems whenever appropriate.

Important materials may be used across GregTech, Modern Industrialization, Create, Mekanism, and Applied Energistics 2.

Material progression must follow the technological tiers.

Higher-tier materials should require increasingly complex processing chains.

Materials from one mod should not provide unrestricted access to higher-tier materials from another mod.

Cross-mod material processing may be required for advanced components.

Machine Progression

Machines should follow the main technological progression.

Machine access must depend on the appropriate tier, materials, power infrastructure, and prerequisite machines.

Machines from different mods may be required to produce components for each other.

A machine from one mod should not completely replace the intended function of another mod's progression.

Specialized machines should remain useful because they provide unique processing methods or production advantages.

Power Progression

Power generation and distribution must follow technological progression.

Early progression should rely on primitive and mechanical power systems.

Steam should establish the first reliable industrial power infrastructure.

Electrical tiers should progressively increase available power and machine capacity.

Higher-tier machines must require appropriately advanced power infrastructure.

Power generation should not allow early access to machines from higher technological tiers.

Automation Progression

Automation should evolve alongside technological progression.

Early automation should be limited and primarily mechanical.

Steam automation should introduce larger continuous production systems.

Electrical tiers should enable increasingly complex automated factories.

Advanced tiers should support highly parallelized production, complex processing chains, and large logistics networks.

Applied Energistics 2 should become increasingly important for high-level digital logistics and automated crafting.

Automation should reduce repetitive work without removing progression requirements.

Resource Progression

Resources should become increasingly difficult to process as technological progression advances.

Early resources should be accessible through basic methods.

Advanced resources should require increasingly complex mining, processing, chemical treatment, alloying, or purification.

Exploration resources should remain relevant throughout the progression.

Rare materials should be used to create meaningful progression gates rather than simply increasing recipe costs.

Resource production should eventually require industrial infrastructure rather than manual processing.

GregTech Integration

GregTech defines the primary technological progression.

Its materials, machines, components, and voltage tiers provide the main structure for industrial advancement.

Other mods should connect to GregTech progression through materials, components, machines, processing chains, logistics, and automation.

Modern Industrialization Integration

Modern Industrialization provides complementary industrial systems.

Its machines and processing chains should connect to the appropriate GregTech progression tiers.

MI should provide additional production methods without creating a separate route to the endgame.

Create Integration

Create provides mechanical processing, logistics, transportation, and physical automation.

Create should be particularly important during the Primitive and Steam Ages.

Later tiers may continue to use Create for logistics and specialized mechanical infrastructure.

Create should complement electrical technology rather than replace it.

Mekanism Integration

Mekanism provides specialized chemical processing, material processing, energy systems, and industrial utilities.

Its advanced systems should require appropriate technological progression.

Mekanism should interact with GregTech and Modern Industrialization materials without becoming an independent progression path.

Applied Energistics 2 Integration

Applied Energistics 2 provides advanced digital logistics and automation.

AE2 progression should be gated behind appropriate technological infrastructure.

Advanced storage, automated crafting, and large-scale logistics should require increasingly advanced components.

AE2 should automate production but should not eliminate the need for the machines and factories producing the required materials.

Create Aeronautics Integration

Create Aeronautics should connect aerial engineering to the industrial progression.

Aircraft and advanced aerial systems should require industrial materials, mechanical components, and appropriate technological infrastructure.

Aeronautics should expand transportation and exploration without bypassing technological progression.

Create Big Cannons Integration

Create Big Cannons should connect heavy artillery to industrial manufacturing.

Advanced cannons, ammunition, and components should require increasingly advanced materials and manufacturing infrastructure.

Artillery progression should remain dependent on the main industrial progression.

Cross-Mod Production Chains

Advanced components should frequently require multiple production systems.

A component may require:

GregTech materials

Modern Industrialization processing

Mekanism chemical processing

Create mechanical processing

Applied Energistics 2 logistics

The exact chains should be established during recipe development.

Progression Gates

Important technological milestones must have clear prerequisites.

A progression gate may require:

A previous technological tier

Specific machines

Specific materials

Specific processing capabilities

A required power infrastructure

A required automation system

A required cross-mod component

Progression gates should prevent players from obtaining late-game technology through isolated or unintended routes.

Progression Integrity

No recipe should provide an unintended shortcut through the main progression.

Recipes that allow early access to higher-tier materials, machines, tools, power systems, storage systems, or automation must be modified or removed.

Mod-specific progression should always respect the global progression structure.

Endgame Integration

At the highest conventional tiers, the different technology systems should become increasingly interconnected.

Late-game production should require large industrial infrastructure, advanced logistics, high-capacity power systems, complex processing chains, and extensive automation.

Post-endgame systems such as ProjectE and Avaritia should build upon this infrastructure rather than replace it.

Implementation

The integration defined in this document will be implemented through recipe changes, progression gates, custom components, machine requirements, resource requirements, and cross-mod production chains.

KubeJS will be used to implement the required recipe modifications and progression restrictions.

GuideME will document the resulting progression and explain the relationships between the different technological systems.
